**Batch it, don't send one giant insert or loop per-row.** Slicing your array into chunks (e.g. 500 rows) and calling `.insert(batch)` in a loop is the documented pattern (`apps/docs/content/guides/storage/vector/storing-vectors.mdx`, "Batch processing large datasets"):

```js
const BATCH_SIZE = 500
for (let i = 0; i < dbData.length; i += BATCH_SIZE) {
  const batch = dbData.slice(i, i + BATCH_SIZE)
  const { error } = await supabase.from('player_game_logs').insert(batch)
  if (error) console.error(`Batch failed at offset ${i}:`, error)
}
```

Per-row inserts are the worst option (one round-trip each = 55k+ requests). If you still hit query timeouts on large batches, see `apps/docs/content/guides/database/import-data.mdx`, "2. Increase statement timeouts" — you can raise the statement timeout, but 500-row batches usually avoid needing that.

